config XIAOMI_METIS
	tristate "Xiaomi METIS stock reconstruction (6.18 aligned)"
	depends on ARM64 && ANDROID_VENDOR_HOOKS && ANDROID_VENDOR_OEM_DATA
	default n
	help
	  Xiaomi METIS fully aligned to the CCC dash reconstruction
	  (OS3.0.305 stock): VIP/lock-inheritance marking, cold-start
	  protection, cluster affinity/frequency boost, pick-side policy
	  libraries, WALT/deadline/schlat/io/lowlt faces and the registry
	  provider slots, all attached to the live 6.18 GKI vendor-hook
	  surface. Closed-scheduler-only entry bridges (stock-context
	  assembly) are kept compiled but dormant, matching upstream dash.
	  Carrier state lives in the mi_schedule task slots. Stock defects
	  are retained except where the 6.18 environment forbids them
	  (mutex oem payload co-tenancy with xr_qi, record_*_starttime
	  hook absence, set_next_entity signature drift).
